• Strongly Typed Configuration: Use the Options pattern (IOptions<T>) to map your
configuration values to strongly typed objects for easier access and type safety.
• Environment-Specific Settings: Use appsettings.{Environment}.json files to store
configuration values that vary depending on the environment (Development, Production,
etc.).
• Secret Management: Store sensitive information (e.g., passwords, API keys) in Azure Key
Vault or other secure storage mechanisms.
• Layered Configuration: Combine multiple configuration sources (files, environment
variables, etc.) with a well-defined order of precedence.
• Reload On Change: Consider using reloadOnChange: true in your configuration providers to
automatically reload configuration changes without restarting the application.
